      "answer": "$p=-4$, $q=-3$",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "Gradient $AB=\\frac12$ — B1, SOI. Intersect $y=-2x+4$ with the line through $(8,3)$ of gradient $\\frac12$: $-2x+4=\\frac12(x-8)+3$, solve to $x=2,y=0$ — *M1. Use midpoint: $\\frac{8+p}{2}=2$ or $\\frac{3+q}{2}=0$ — DM1. $p=-4,q=-3$ — A1. Alternative: equate $\\frac{q-3}{p-8}=\\frac12$ and use midpoint in the perpendicular-bisector equation — *M1; solve simultaneous linear equations — DM1; same answer — A1. A further equivalent line-equation route is accepted. Total: 4.",
